00:00:05.082 --> 00:00:06.040
DINO CHIESA: Dino here.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.020
In the prior videos
in this series,

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:13.270
we learned the how and why of
API proxies and API products.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:17.590
In this video, we'll learn
about the API portal.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.170
The Apigee Edge developer
portal is the best way

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:23.560
to connect developers
who use APIs to the APIs

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.360
you've created.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.320
It includes an elegant
web experience,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.409
clear interactive
API documentation,

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:36.580
and a self-service way to
get credentials or keys.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.770
However delightful
your APIs are,

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.770
if developers cannot
easily get access to them,

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.170
if they cannot easily
understand how to use them,

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.390
adoption will suffer.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:50.380
The Apigee Edge developer
portal addresses that need.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.290
Via the portal, API
providers can publish

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.870
a catalog of API products.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:00.310
API consumers, developers of
the apps that invoke the APIs,

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:04.340
can learn about the available
APIs and begin using them.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:06.220
So let's see it working.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.640
First I'll assume the
role of API provider.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.170
Sign into apigee.com.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.730
Click on this portals link.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:19.820
Plus portal will
create a new portal.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.740
Name it.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.110
Clicking through, I
can manage that portal.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.050
This page gives access to
the theme, the portal pages,

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:36.800
various settings, and assets
like images and so on.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.000
But let's see what
the portal looks like.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.870
We'll click on the live portal
link and see the sample.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.080
This is what API consumer
developers would see.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.690
Now, this is just the sample.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.030
You'll want to
change your portal.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.940
Let's flip back to
the administrative UI,

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.830
once again, assuming the
role of API publisher.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:09.860
Let's make some quick changes,
first, the logo image, the hero

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:15.525
image, a custom diagram.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:21.710
Here I've uploaded
only image assets.

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:24.200
You can, of course, add
assets of other types.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.410
Now the theme--

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:32.470
I have full control over
the CSS for the site,

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:35.410
so you can brand it
any way you like.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:40.490
I'll just paste my own
CSS in and publish that.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:52.850
Some text for the homepage,
I'll publish that.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.440
Text for the getting
started page--

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:01.445
and publish.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.890
OK, let's see what we've got.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.640
That looks pretty good.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.610
Let's click around here.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:16.740
We can see the getting started
page, a link to support.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.650
Now, in your portal, you
can define the menu here

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.150
and the pages they open.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.800
In this video, you
learned the basics

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.710
of API portals and the basics
for styling your portal

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.000
and adding your own content.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.810
You can also publish
APIs to the portal.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.140
We haven't done that yet.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.530
That's a topic for
the next video.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.060
Until then, keep it digital.

